{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/scanbotsdk\/scanbotui\/defaultimagestoreencrypter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]},{"paths":["\/documentation\/scanbotsdk\/scanbotui\/defaultimagestoreencrypter"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The SBSDKUI-component-wide encrypter for storing image data to disk. Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK\/ScanbotUI\/defaultImageStoreEncrypter"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK","doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK\/ScanbotUI"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultImageStoreEncrypter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:@M@ScanbotSDK@objc(pl)SBSDKStorageCrypting","identifier":"doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK\/SBSDKStorageCrypting","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SBSDKStorageCrypting"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If set to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" no encryption is used at all.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use the built-in encrypter "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK\/SBSDKAESEncrypter","type":"reference"},{"text":" to encrypt your sensitive image data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"using AES128 or AES256 before storing it to disk.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"When using encryption you still can access the unencrypted images in the image storage.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Of course, encrypted storages cannot be read without the proper encrypter being set here.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"You are responsible for migrating image storages."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you wish to use the ScanbotSDK RTU-UI-wide encryption setup your encrypter before using any of the ScanbotSDK RTU-UI API."}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A good place to configure it, is your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppDelegate"},{"type":"text","text":"’s entry point, right where the license is set."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Once ScanbotSDK RTU-UI API is used the storages are created and any change to the default encrypter is of no effect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For standard components, prefixed with SBSDK (without UI) the default encrypter has no effect, since there is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no image storage by default. You can, of course, create instances of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK\/SBSDKKeyedImageStorage","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/net.doo.ScanbotSDK\/documentation\/ScanbotSDK\/SBSDKIndexedImageStorage"},{"text":" and initialize them with an encrypter of your choice.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"c:@M@ScanbotSDK@objc(cs)ScanbotUI(cpy)defaultImageStoreEncrypter","roleHeading":"Type Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text"